{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"996f19e3-70bf-4dcc-be56-83fdf14c5fbb","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have resolved the prompt caching eviction issue.\n\n### Root Cause\nPreviously in [`bot.py`](file:///tmp/h-abOAcZ/bot.py#L130-L134), `build_system(a, today)` concatenated the static coaching instructions ([`INSTRUCTIONS`](file:///tmp/h-abOAcZ/bot.py#L74-L114)) and the athlete's dynamic details ([`athlete_context(a, today)`](file:///tmp/h-abOAcZ/bot.py#L117-L127)) into a single text block marked with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`. Whenever `save_fact` was executed, new facts mutated `athlete_context`, altering the entire combined text block and invalidating the cache prefix for the full system prompt on the next call.\n\n### Solution\nIn [`bot.py`](file:///tmp/h-abOAcZ/bot.py#L130-L136), [`build_system`](file:///tmp/h-abOAcZ/bot.py#L130-L136) was modified to split the system prompt into two separate text blocks:\n1. **Static Coaching Instructions Block**: Contains `INSTRUCTIONS` with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`.\n2. **Dynamic Context Block**: Contains `athlete_context(a, today)` without cache control.\n\nBecause the stable prefix containing `INSTRUCTIONS` remains unchanged when facts are appended or across requests, Claude can read the static coaching instructions from cache without eviction.\n\nThe details of the fix have been documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-abOAcZ/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":78.478461,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":127494,"output_tokens":2553,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":285148,"total_tokens":130047}}}
